# --- Generated ---
# `packages/api-client-ts/src/generated/schema.ts` is the only file
# under `generated/`. It IS committed — the `openapi-drift` CI job
# regenerates it from the live OpenAPI spec and fails the build if
# the committed copy is out of sync. Web-side typecheck depends on
# the committed copy too. Keep this directory tracked.

# --- Local agent/tool working state ---
# Local tool state is never committed. This repo is PUBLIC: agent
# configuration routinely names internal paths, hosts, workflows and
# review habits, none of which belong in a public history, and none of
# which the app or CI needs to build. The patterns below were lost at
# some point (the comments survived, the rules did not), which left
# every one of these paths merely untracked rather than ignored — one
# `git add -A` away from being published. Guarded in CI by the
# "No agent files" job in ci.yml.
.claude/
.agents/
.codex/
.serena/
.superpowers/
.cursor/
.windsurf/
.aider*
.mcp.json
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md
.github/copilot-instructions.md
docs/superpowers/

# Codex credential-provisioning notes. Describes a local machine layout
# (%USERPROFILE%\.codex\*.env) and how to scope a disposable test
# account — operator runbook for agent tooling, not product docs.
SECURITY_SETUP.md

# Notes produced by the agent's brainstorming workflow stay local per
# developer.

# Top-level design-bundle landing dir (separate from the
# fetches here when working on an audit).
/_fetched/

# Self-contained brand-book exports (inline-assets HTML, ~7 MB).
# Generated from the brand pack source for external sharing; the
# tracked About.html and brand pack source files are the canonical
# inputs. Keep these out of git history to avoid blob bloat.
docs/*.standalone.html

# AI-assisted planning artifacts (specs/plans/runbooks). Internal dev
# process output, not product or contributor docs — keep out of the
# public repo. Local copies are fine; they just never get tracked.
# (This entry previously read "the release design notes", a prose
# fragment that matched nothing.)
docs/specs/
docs/plans/

# Opt-in widget-audit measurement output (AUDIT=1), not a build artefact.
apps/web/reports/

# Review images left over from the projection port. Nothing regenerates
# these any more -- the screenshot-only capture cases that wrote them were
# removed once the port was judged -- but the files are still on disk and
# are 8 MB of local scratch. Ignored so they stay out of `git status`;
# delete the directory when it has served its purpose.
apps/web/.playwright-captures/
